Z||000000||The Fieromaster||06-07-2001||04:07 AM||||I am not to sure what is behind the PONTIAC to make it light RED but i was thinking about removing it and instaling either a colored vynal piece to make it another color (yellow in my case) OR leaving it clear and putting one of those neon tubes in there instead of the bulbs... What does the lights look like apart?  I dont want to destroy mine if they arent re-assembleable!<P>If all goes well i just MIGHT try making a clear light system like the Aleza's that the rice boys have! hmmm how cool would that be!!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">   <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||11
Z||000001||tgowens||06-07-2001||04:10 AM||||that's a red plastic insert behind the clear lens.........the lens will come off of the light unit but be careful when prying up the plastic clips as they will break easily. Generally the lens is also held on by a silicone type compound<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>                 <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/3GTS_SIG.gif">                  </A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||The Fieromaster||06-07-2001||04:23 AM||||what gives the lenses the black outlines?  Is taht painted on?  Inside or outside?  If i can remove that and polish the lenses clear it would be a GREAT start on the clear tail lights!  That i would LOVE to have... cause it would look like my eclipse did with Aleza' (didnt have em but wanted em)<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">   <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||06-07-2001||04:27 AM||||the black is actually a laminated plastic coating on the inside of the lens - usually you will see where thay have started to de-laminate on some of the older lenses - kinda makes it look like there is an air bubble in there........once you remove the lens from the housing you will see a red insert for the tail light, the "pontiac" light and an amber insert for the turn signal light........<P>hope this helps......||||reg||1
Z||000004||RiceCooker||06-07-2001||10:28 AM||||Don't know too much about it but a friend of mine had his bulbs (i think) painted yellow to match his car colour. Well, needless to say, it looks awesome - especially at night.||||reg||6
